Recent Earnings Highlights
CG Oncology (
CGON
)
-0.8% Last 3m
CG Oncology Inc is a late-stage clinical biopharmaceutical company focused on=
 developing and commercializing its product candidate, cretostimogene grenade=
norepvec, for patients with bladder cancer. The company's candidate, cretosti=
mogene grenadenorepvec, is a targeted oncolytic intravesically delivered immu=
notherapy agent that is in two phase three trials (one high-risk BCG unrespon=
sive NMIBC trial and one intermediate-risk NMIBC trial) and a phase two clini=
cal study with a checkpoint inhibitor for high-risk BCG unresponsive NMIBC di=
sease.
Reported:
November 12, 2026 =C2=B7
Google Finance earnings page
At a Glance
CG Oncology Outperforms Financial Estimates:
The company reported an Adjusted EPS loss of $0.64, outperforming the estimat=
ed loss of $0.81, and delivered total revenue of $1.60 million, beating the e=
stimated $0.53 million.
R&D Spending Rises Amid Pipeline Expansion:
Research and development expenses increased 41% year-over-year to $39.22 mill=
ion, reflecting intensified clinical trial activity for its oncology pipeline=
 compared to past periods.
Substantial Funding Expected Through 2029:
The company highlighted a strong cash runway, with $984.5 million in cash, ca=
sh equivalents, and marketable securities, which is projected to fund its cli=
nical operations through 2029.
Major Regulatory Submission Planned for Q4:
CG Oncology expects to complete its Biologics License Application (BLA) submi=
ssion for cretostimogene in BCG-unresponsive non-muscle-invasive bladder canc=
er (NMIBC) in the fourth quarter of 2026.
Imminent Clinical Trial Data Readouts Anticipated:
Topline Phase 3 data from the PIVOT-006 trial are expected in November 2026, =
followed by 12-month data cohorts from BOND-003 and CORE-008 trials in Decemb=
er 2026.
Positive Market Reaction Pushes Shares Higher:
Following the better-than-expected financial metrics and upcoming catalyst co=
nfirmations, investor enthusiasm drove the stock price higher, hitting an int=
raday peak of $80.03.
Ionis Pharmaceuticals (
IONS
)
-49.2% Last 3m
Ionis Pharmaceuticals is the leading developer of antisense technology to dis=
cover and develop novel drugs. Its broad clinical and preclinical pipeline ta=
rgets a wide variety of diseases, with an emphasis on cardiovascular, metabol=
ic, neurological, and rare diseases. Ionis and Biogen brought Spinraza to mar=
ket in 2016 as a treatment for spinal muscular atrophy, and Biogen launched A=
LS drug Qalsody in 2023. Ionis brought two additional drugs to market via its=
 cardiovascular-focused subsidiary Akcea, including ATTR amyloidosis drug Teg=
sedi (2018) and cardiology drug Waylivra (Europe, 2019). Ionis and AstraZenec=
a launched polyneuropathy drug Wainua in 2024. Ionis marked its first two ind=
ependent launches in 2025 for Tryngolza (for FCS) and Dawnzera (for HAE).
Reported:
November 11, 2026 =C2=B7
Google Finance earnings page
Earnings Call Summary
Ionis reported strong financial results for Q3 2026, with revenue reaching $2=
43 million, marking a 55% year-over-year increase compared to the same period=
 last year (excluding a prior one-time payment). Commercial revenue grew 18% =
year-over-year to $136 million, outpacing R&D revenue, driven primarily by st=
rong momentum from DAWNZERA product sales.
At a Glance
Ionis Beats EPS and Revenue Estimates:
Ionis Pharmaceuticals reported a reported adjusted EPS of $0 and a reported r=
evenue of $242,721,000, strongly beating estimated adjusted EPS of -$0.934 an=
d estimated revenue of $184,375,930.
Commercial Revenue Driven by DAWNZERA Growth:
Total commercial revenue reached $136 million for the quarter, up 18% year-ov=
er-year, heavily supported by DAWNZERA product sales which brought in $37 mil=
lion, up 40% from the previous quarter.
TRYNGOLZA Forecast Slashed While Reaffirming Guidance:
The company slashed full-year 2026 sales guidance for TRYNGOLZA to approximat=
ely $50 million due to a slower-than-expected launch ramp, though it maintain=
ed overall total revenue guidance of $875 million to $900 million.
Cash Flow Breakeven Target Pushed Back:
Management pushed its target timeline for sustained positive cash flow by one=
 year from 2028 to 2029, citing the gradual TRYNGOLZA rollout and clinical Ph=
ase III disappointments in partnered programs.
Stock Plummets Amid Mixed Launch Progress:
Despite delivering a headline earnings beat, the stock plummeted nearly 28% a=
s investors reacted with disappointment over commercial trial roadblocks and =
slower product adoption updates.
Ocular therapeutix (
OCUL
)
-38.1% Last 3m
Ocular Therapeutix Inc is a biotechnology company that specializes in therapi=
es for diseases and conditions of the eye. The company uses its proprietary h=
ydrogel platform technology to deliver therapeutic agents to the eye. Its pip=
eline consists of eye medication that aims to overcome the limitations of cur=
rent eye-drop-based therapies for ophthalmic diseases and conditions. Its pip=
eline product includes Dextenza, OTX-TIC, OTX-TKI, and OTX-IVT.
Reported:
November 9, 2026 =C2=B7
Google Finance earnings page
Reported Results
Q3 2026: EPS -$0.42 vs. -$0.35 est. (-19.59%); revenue $12.87M vs. $14.30M es=
t. (-9.96%)
